Scope of this license

This CC BY 4.0 license applies to the following top-level entries of this public cut:
  - `.gitignore` — repository housekeeping file
  - `01_response/` — pre-registrations, scripts, rating records and results of the revision studies and re-counts
  - `CHECKSUMS.sha256` — SHA-256 checksums of the files of this cut
  - `CITATION.cff` — citation metadata of this cut
  - `MANIFEST.csv` — every file of the reviewer version (path, SHA-256, size, top-level folder) with its status in
    this cut (`public_cut`) and, for files present here, their SHA-256 here (`public_sha256`); files only in this cut
    are added at the end
  - `README.md` — deposit-level README
  - `REVISION_R1.md` — record of the changes made for the first-round revision (R1)
  - `RUNNING.md` — how the stages were run
  - `application_direction_chemontology_layer_a/` — EP-to-ChemOntology mapping (application direction)
  - `future_work_pointers/` — records of planned follow-up studies
  - `papers/` — run records of the control experiments, the held-out set, the single-prompt baselines, the input ablation and the audits of the revision
  - `supporting_information/` — the revised Supporting Information (`SI_R1.pdf`)
  - `tier_1_prompt_versions/` — the UQS prompts
  - `tier_2_input_metadata/` — corpus manifest
  - `tier_4_classification_tables/` — classification tables, figure data and rendered figures
  - `tier_5_retrieval_logs/` — retrieval audit logs and queries
  - `tier_6_audit_decisions/` — audit decisions
  - `tier_7_aggregation_scripts_and_methodology_evolution/` — aggregation and figure scripts, regression log, changelogs
  - `tier_8_redacted_public_raw_outputs/` — redacted copies of the Markdown stage outputs of Tier 3 (the same files in this package and in the public cut)
  - `tier_9_full_raw_logs_reviewer_only/` — README of the reviewer-only tier
  - `zenodo_manifest.md` — deposit manifest

This license does NOT apply to:
  - The source chemistry papers analysed by UQS (these are NOT redistributed here; see
    tier_2_input_metadata/paperA_21_paper_corpus_manifest.csv for the 21-paper corpus
    DOIs and copyright holders).
  - Verbatim source-paper quotations inside the analysis outputs. They are kept for verification
    in the reviewer version of the deposit (Tier 3 / Tier 9 and the per-reference catalogue;
    access restricted to the editor and reviewers until acceptance) and replaced, in Tier 8 and in
    the public cut, by `[REDACTED: …]` markers that point to the source paper (via its DOI or the
    item's `loc:` field) or to the reviewer version.
  - Web of Science records in tier_5_retrieval_logs/ (Clarivate data; reproduced to document the
    retrieval audit, as bibliographic identification fields only in the public cut).
  - Bibliographic-field excerpts (titles, author names, journal names, DOIs) that
    appear in metadata files: these are factual bibliographic data and are reproduced
    for verification purposes.

